WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.702
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-winning

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:05.538
and a Tony-nominated actress,
comedian, writer and producer.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.206
You can see her
alongside Amy Poehler

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:09.809
on their Restless Leg Tour.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.578
She's also back
with a brand-new take

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:14.313
on the beloved movie
"Mean Girls,"

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:16.082
which opens in theaters
January 12th.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.250
Let's take a look.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.452
-May I have
everyone's attention, please?

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:21.587
Eyes to the front of the room.

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:24.757
You may notice we have
a new student joining us today.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:26.492
She just moved here
from Kentucky.

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:27.627
-Kenya.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.996
-Kenya. Her name is "Caddy."

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.764
-It's Cady. Cady Heron.

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:34.433
-My apologies.
I will commit that to memory.

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:37.870
Cady, like the Canadian
songstress KD Lang,

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.605
and Heron,

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:41.574
like the illegal street drug.

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.576
Thank you, "Caddy."

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:46.045
-It's Cady.
-Cady, hi, I'm Ms. Norbury.

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.815
I'll be your homeroom teacher.
This is your roster.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.583
I see also have you
for AP Calculus.

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.852
You must have had excellent
teachers at your old school.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.454
-Oh, I was home schooled.
-Home schooled?

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:57.423
Oh, that's a fun way
to take jobs from my union.

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:59.125
No, I'm joking. That's fine.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.159
-Please welcome back
to the show

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:01.961
our very good friend Tina Fey!

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.963
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:19.478 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:19.478 --> 00:01:22.014
Hello, friend!
-Hello, pal of mine.

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:24.884
-So, it's crazy. Yesterday
David Chase was on the show

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.786
and we were talking about
how it's 25 years

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:27.953
since "The Sopranos" came out.

00:01:27.953 --> 00:01:29.522
That seemed right to me.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.924
20 years since "Mean Girls" --
seems crazy

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:33.426
that it's been 20 years.
-It's crazy because

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.694
David Chase and I
were together at that time.

00:01:35.694 --> 00:01:37.063
-You were dating?
-Yeah. No.

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:40.499
-[ Laughs ]
-Yeah. It's 20 years.

00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:43.069
One of the actresses
in the movie,

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.871
a beautiful actress
named Avantika,

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.572
plays Karen in the movie...

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:49.842
♪ She was not born
when the movie came out ♪

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:53.112
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, boy.

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:54.547
Those are the tough ones.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:55.781
-When they haven't
been born yet.

00:01:55.781 --> 00:01:57.116
But it was very cool.

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:59.552
At the premiere,
Lindsay Lohan showed up,

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:02.355
which is so exciting and cool.
-Yes! Oh, so great.

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.956
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.825
So great to see her.
She looks gorgeous.

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.594
It was so wonderful of her
to come and bless the movie.

00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:09.928
-It was.
It was a nice blessing.

00:02:09.928 --> 00:02:12.332
And I'm sure people are just
so thrilled to see her.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.999
-Yes.
-We also have photos

00:02:13.999 --> 00:02:16.502
because, again, when you went to
the premiere of your movie,

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:18.238
this is you 20 years ago...
-Okay.

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:20.373
-...at the premiere
of the film "Mean Girls."

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.641
-Sure.
-And here you are now.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:22.875
20 years ago.

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:26.713
And let me just say...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:29.616
...it's like you look
so much less clumsy.

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:31.050
-I mean, what...

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.220
First of all, oh,
do I miss the buccal fat, right,

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.488
that was in my face.

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:38.891
And also, like,
clearly could not walk in heels

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:40.326
even for one hot second.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.295
-Yeah.
-Like, am I falling?

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.396
-No, it's really --
This is when you definitely

00:02:44.396 --> 00:02:46.432
"writer came first."
-Writer came first.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:49.301
I thought I was doing like a
full runway-quality walk

00:02:49.301 --> 00:02:50.937
in that moment.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.772
Look at my, like, chunky
'90s highlights.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.674
-That's the way
you walk in an attic.

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.376
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:59.111
-And this lady looks like a...
-She's graceful.

00:02:59.111 --> 00:03:02.681
-...scary lady
from a soap opera whose, like,

00:03:02.681 --> 00:03:05.151
family have taken
over the hospital

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:06.919
and are going to turn it
into a nightclub.

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:08.921
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:11.090
I do want to do one more
before and after.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.558
It's a little bit later,
but this is --

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:14.694
we've now gone -- as writers,

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:15.828
we've gone through
two writers strikes.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:18.831
-Yes.
-Here we are in 2007.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.700
Look at those two.
-What's going on?

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.402
-And, yeah, that's like we --
it was like

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:24.003
we found out that morning
about the strike.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.504
We're like, "What?"
-"What?"

00:03:25.504 --> 00:03:27.306
-And then here we are.
Look at us.

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:29.141
We're out on the road.
-We're still on strike.

00:03:29.141 --> 00:03:31.144
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:33.913
With Freddie.
-You, uh --

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.581
You know this, um...

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:38.417
You know our producer
at this show, Mike Shoemaker.

00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:39.585
-Yeah.
-He's still mad at me

00:03:39.585 --> 00:03:42.588
for that hat.
-Yeah, I mean, I get it.

00:03:42.588 --> 00:03:44.423
I mean, we think --
I think this picture ended up

00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:47.326
on "The New York Times"
or something, right?

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:50.095
Wow, wow, wow, wow, wow.
So much happening.

00:03:50.095 --> 00:03:51.864
-Yeah.
-Put them side by side.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.367
Like, I wish I could --
I want so badly

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.402
to use the phrase "glow up,"

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.870
but I don't think
we got there.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.272
-[ Laughs ] Yeah, no.
-I don't think we look

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:02.141
like we have any more money now.
-No.

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:04.943
[ Laughter ]
Or we learned any lessons.

00:04:04.943 --> 00:04:07.613
It's like, remember that photo
of us that everybody saw?

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:09.348
-No, and if this
ever happens again,

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:12.919
dress up and smile.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:15.354
-We didn't do it.
-One of the things

00:04:15.354 --> 00:04:17.890
you had to do with the script,

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:21.594
I'm assuming, 20 years later,
is update the slang.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:22.962
-Yes. Yes and no.

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:25.331
I mean, yeah, so we -- the slang
in the movie, I sort of --

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:28.367
The research I did the first
time around with "Mean Girls,"

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:29.702
I talked to a bunch of --
actually

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.871
like a bunch of Long Island
teens where my resource,

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:33.306
and I remember thinking, like,

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.841
oh, whatever they're telling me
is slang now will be gone

00:04:35.841 --> 00:04:37.242
by the time
the movie comes out,

00:04:37.242 --> 00:04:38.444
and I'll look like a fool.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:41.080
-[ Laughs ]
-So I tried to avoid slang.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.382
I, we sort of made up
the word "fetch," you know,

00:04:43.382 --> 00:04:47.086
and then my favorite thing
is to -- I like to write kids

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:49.021
talking like they're -- 'cause
sometimes I think it's funny

00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:51.557
when teenagers talk like they're
being pulled over by cops.

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:52.992
Like, you know
when they'll be like,

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:55.327
"Uh, there were some people
there who did have alcohol,

00:04:55.327 --> 00:04:56.995
but what we felt" --
Like, I just like, you know...

00:04:56.995 --> 00:05:00.833
Like, so they mostly talk
the way they speak to adults.

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:02.634
-That's a very good way
of looking at it.

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:04.136
-Yeah.
-You and I,

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:06.839
I think both because of
when our careers started,

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:08.374
we've been writing comedy
for a long time.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.076
-Yeah.
-Are there things you go back

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:12.178
and look at ever
and are like, "Oh, boy"?

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:13.512
-Oh. Only everything.
-Yeah.

00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:14.647
-Yeah. Like, yeah.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.849
What a gift to
get to reopen this movie

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:20.486
and just, like, quietly just
hide -- remove some things.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:23.222
I get to, like, clean the gums.
-Yeah.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:25.491
-Yeah, I -- There --

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:27.559
Well, first of all, there's
a platform called Peacock.

00:05:27.559 --> 00:05:30.396
Second of all, they --
On Peacock,

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:31.597
there is a channel

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:33.799
that's just an "SNL" channel...
-Yes.

00:05:33.799 --> 00:05:36.569
-...that just shows
just random "SNL" sketches,

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:39.638
and they are -- they do not seem
to be curated in any way.

00:05:39.638 --> 00:05:41.808
-Yeah.
-It's just like someone had,

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:43.843
like, an old Rubbermaid tub

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:44.910
and they're like,
"Shake 'em out!"

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.345
-The Peacock tagline is

00:05:46.345 --> 00:05:47.814
"We don't know
what it's going to be either."

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:50.083
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:51.884
-So sometimes I like to put this

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:55.054
on when we're having dinner
as a family and, uh, you know,

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:57.656
and you get, like, a great
classic Will Ferrell sketch

00:05:57.656 --> 00:06:00.526
and then like a weird, like,
Charles Rocket "Update" feature.

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:01.727
You just never know
what's going to happen.

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:03.196
-Yeah.
-And there'll be --

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:06.065
Something will come on that's
just like, one, not playing,

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:08.234
two, definitely problematic.

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:10.002
And my kids will be like,
"Oh, wow."

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:12.538
And I'm sitting there knowing
that I full-tilt wrote it

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:15.608
and I'm just like...
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:16.576
Like...

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:19.679
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:20.813
I don't tell them.

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:23.015
-I have a ton more questions
for you.

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:25.051
We'll be right back
with more Tina after this.

